---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import UploadArea from '../../components/UploadArea.astro';
import Kitty from '../../components/Kitty.astro';
---
<ToolLayout title="Image converter" description="Same image. A fresh format. Convert JPG, PNG, and WebP right in your browser, with a little help from Loki.">
<noscript><p class="noscript">This tool needs JavaScript to convert images locally. Enable it in your browser and reload to get started.</p></noscript>
<section class="workspace" id="converter" aria-label="Image converter"><div class="workspace-top"><div class="workflow" aria-label="Conversion steps"><span data-step="upload" class="active">01 Select</span><span data-step="editor">02 Convert</span><span data-step="result">03 Download</span></div><span class="tool-badge">● Private by design</span></div><p id="tool-status" class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
<UploadArea />
<div id="editor-panel" class="state-panel" hidden><div class="editor-grid"><div class="preview-wrap"><img id="input-preview" alt="Selected image preview" /></div><div><h2 id="file-name" class="file-name"></h2><p id="file-meta" class="file-meta"></p><label class="field-label" for="output-name">Save file as</label><div class="filename-control"><input id="output-name" type="text" maxlength="100" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" aria-describedby="filename-help" /><span id="file-extension">.webp</span></div><p id="filename-help" class="field-hint">Choose a name. We add the correct file extension.</p><label class="field-label" for="output-format">Convert to</label><select id="output-format"><option value="image/webp">WebP — smaller, web-friendly</option><option value="image/jpeg">JPG — widely compatible</option><option value="image/png">PNG — lossless, transparent</option></select><div id="quality-field"><label class="field-label" for="quality">Quality <output id="quality-value" for="quality">85%</output></label><input type="range" id="quality" min="10" max="100" value="85" step="1" /><p class="field-hint">Higher quality can mean a larger file.</p></div><p class="field-hint mt-4" id="format-hint">Transparency is preserved. Animated inputs become a still image.</p><div class="editor-actions"><button id="convert" class="button">Convert image <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button><button class="text-link" data-reset>Choose another</button></div></div></div></div>
<div id="processing-panel" class="state-panel processing-panel" hidden><Kitty small interactive={false} /><span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2>A little format magic…</h2><p>Loki is working on your image, right here on your device.</p></div>
<div id="result-panel" class="state-panel result-panel" hidden><Kitty small interactive={false} /><h2 tabindex="-1" id="result-title">All done. Nicely converted.</h2><p>Your image is ready for its next adventure.</p><div class="preview-wrap"><img id="output-preview" alt="Converted image preview" /></div><div id="result-meta" class="result-meta"></div><a id="download" class="button" download>Download image <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><div><button class="text-link mt-3" data-reset>Convert another image ↗</button></div></div>
<div id="error-panel" class="state-panel error-panel" hidden><Kitty small interactive={false} /><h2 tabindex="-1" id="error-title">A little snag.</h2><p id="error-message" class="error-message"></p><button class="button" data-reset>Try another image <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button></div>
</section>
<section class="tool-details"><h2>A few helpful details.</h2><details><summary>Does my image leave my device?</summary><p>No. Your browser handles the conversion. KittySuite never uploads or stores your image, and there’s no account to create.</p></details><details><summary>Which format should I choose?</summary><p>JPG works well for photographs and broad compatibility. PNG preserves image detail and transparency without lossy compression. WebP supports transparency and often makes smaller files for the web. Your browser must support WebP encoding to use that output.</p></details><details><summary>What changes when I convert?</summary><p>The image dimensions stay the same. JPG fills transparent areas with white. Animation becomes a single still frame, and original metadata is not retained. Lossy formats may change detail and color slightly. Output may be larger than your original.</p></details><details><summary>Why is there a file limit?</summary><p>The 20 MB and 16 megapixel limits help keep conversion comfortable on phones. Very large images or browsers with limited memory may still need a smaller source image.</p></details></section>
<script src="../../scripts/converter.ts"></script>
</ToolLayout>